\"transform:none;transform-origin:50% 50%;transform-box:fill-box\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"10.73312629199899\" class=\"_74-EFW_nodeBg\"></circle><image href=\"/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww-cdn.anthropic.com%2Fimages%2F4zrzovbb%2Fwebsite%2F5f8644ad8a7fb9053f991843f0a93d41f2d5acf9-2000x2000.jpg&amp;w=96&amp;q=75\" x=\"-10.73312629199899\" y=\"-10.73312629199899\" width=\"21.46625258399798\" height=\"21.46625258399798\" clip-path=\"url(#_R_19rpbsnpfkq6btb_)\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\"></image></g></g><g transform=\"translate(174.7186933333333, 37.88585806911715)\"><g style=\"transform:none;transform-origin:50% 50%;transform-box:fill-box\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"10.73312629199899\" class=\"_74-EFW_nodeBg\"></circle><image href=\"https://assets.claude.com/16c346d44a310e746657cd16ea275a2da5efa719.png\" x=\"-10.73312629199899\" y=\"-10.73312629199899\" width=\"21.46625258399798\" height=\"21.46625258399798\" clip-path=\"url(#_R_19rpbsnpfkq6btb_)\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\"></image></g></g><g transform=\"translate(134.00833158018932, 78.31119270027229)\"><g style=\"transform:none;transform-origin:50% 50%;transform-box:fill-box\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"10.73312629199899\" class=\"_74-EFW_nodeBg\"></circle><image href=\"https://assets.claude.com/1755639b93c7cec99475de59cb9802d0e13e6207.png\" x=\"-10.73312629199899\" y=\"-10.73312629199899\" width=\"21.46625258399798\" height=\"21.46625258399798\" clip-path=\"url(#_R_19rpbsnpfkq6btb_)\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\"></image></g></g><g transform=\"translate(253.95159999999998, 26.688807299727713)\"><g style=\"transform:none;transform-origin:50% 50%;transform-box:fill-box\"><circle cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" r=\"10.73312629199899\" class=\"_74-EFW_nodeBg\"></circle><image href=\"https://assets.claude.com/18636e2f18982e3166a613b3f028e27b196bfe2f.png\" x=\"-10.73312629199899\" y=\"-10.73312629199899\" width=\"21.46625258399798\" height=\"21.46625258399798\" clip-path=\"url(#_R_19rpbsnpfkq6btb_)\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid slice\"></image></g></g><circle cx=\"98.63074666666667\" cy=\"54.70090460923742\" r=\"16.733126291998992\" fill=\"transparent\" class=\"_74-EFW_nodeHit\"></circle><a aria-label=\"A research agenda for the Economic Futures Research Fund\" href=\"/news/economic-futures-research-fund-agenda\"><circle cx=\"26.048399999999994\" cy=\"65.88964037996826\" r=\"16.733126291998992\" fill=\"transparent\" class=\"_74-EFW_nodeHit\"></circle></a><a aria-label=\"Ben Bernanke appointed to Anthropic’s Long-Term Benefit Trust \" href=\"/news/ben-bernanke\"><circle cx=\"174.7186933333333\" cy=\"37.88585806911715\" r=\"16.733126291998992\" fill=\"transparent\" class=\"_74-EFW_nodeHit\"></circle></a><a aria-label=\"Introducing Claude Corps\" href=\"/news/claude-corps\"><circle cx=\"134.00833158018932\" cy=\"78.31119270027229\" r=\"16.733126291998992\" fill=\"transparent\" class=\"_74-EFW_nodeHit\"></circle></a><a aria-label=\"Introducing the Anthropic Economic Advisory Council \" href=\"/news/introducing-the-anthropic-economic-advisory-council\"><circle cx=\"253.95159999999998\" cy=\"26.688807299727713\" r=\"16.733126291998992\" fill=\"transparent\" class=\"_74-EFW_nodeHit\"></circle></a></svg></div></div><div class=\"tOQyXa_headline-6 yApI1G_headline\" data-component=\"Headline\">Related articles</div><ul class=\"yApI1G_list\"><li><div class=\"yApI1G_card _8J1zJG_card\"><header class=\"_8J1zJG_cardHeader\"><div class=\"_8J1zJG_eyebrowsWrapper\"><p>Announcements</p><p>Jul 22, 2026</p></div></header><div class=\"_8J1zJG_text\" data-lines=\"3\" style=\"--text-lines:3\"><a class=\"_8J1zJG_link\" href=\"/news/economic-futures-research-fund-agenda\">A research agenda for the Economic Futures Research Fund</a></div></div></li></ul><a data-component=\"AnchorButton\" data-variant=\"tertiary\" class=\"f9ZZrG_button f9ZZrG_corner-small f9ZZrG_variant-tertiary f9ZZrG_size-small f9ZZrG_icon-format-trailing yApI1G_cta\" rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/search?topic=funding\">View more<span class=\"f9ZZrG_icon\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"currentColor\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"flex-shrink:0\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M11.1465 4.64648C11.3417 4.45127 11.6582 4.45136 11.8535 4.64648L16.8535 9.64649L16.916 9.72267C16.9703 9.80418 17 9.90061 17 10C17 10.1326 16.9473 10.2598 16.8535 10.3535L11.8535 15.3535C11.6583 15.5486 11.3417 15.5487 11.1465 15.3535C10.9513 15.1583 10.9514 14.8418 11.1465 14.6465L15.293 10.5H3.5C3.2239 10.5 3.00006 10.2761 3 10C3 9.72387 3.22386 9.50001 3.5 9.50001H15.293L11.1465 5.35352C10.9514 5.15826 10.9513 4.8417 11.1465 4.64648Z\"></path></svg></span></a></div></aside></div><div class=\"PA4F1q_body\" data-article-body=\"true\" data-theme=\"ivory\"><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">Today, we’re committing a portion of Anthropic’s shares to the Anthropic Public Benefit Fund,<strong> </strong>a new wholly owned entity with a structure that increases the stake as the company grows. Subject to stockholder approval, 5% of Anthropic’s shares will be committed today, with an additional 2% added at the board’s discretion for every 50% increase in the company’s value above a set baseline.</p><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">As a public benefit corporation, most of our work in pursuit of our mission takes place inside the company: research relevant to AI safety and interpretability; applied biomedical research; discounts on Claude for nonprofits and scientific institutions. These activities have both a public benefit component and for-profit value, so we house them directly in the company.</p><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">The Anthropic Public Benefit Fund will have increased flexibility and scale, enabling us to pursue our mission in new ways: for example, we might explore large donations to traditional nonprofits or direct distributions to specific populations.</p><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">One example is labor market impacts. AI may generate enormous economic value, but it could also cause instability for many workers. Anthropic has already committed <a href=\"/news/economic-futures-research-fund-agenda\">$200 million</a> to studying and addressing this issue, but given the pace of AI progress, bolder approaches may be needed. The Fund will have the versatility to pursue them.</p><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">We’re establishing the Anthropic Public Benefit Fund as an LLC—rather than a 501(c)(3) or other format—to give adjustability between different forms of giving. None of the Anthropic equity held by the LLC will be used for lobbying or political giving, in the US or abroad.</p><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">Because of the way the Fund is structured, the more Anthropic grows, the larger the share of the company that can be dedicated expressly to the public good. It is common practice for tech companies to offer escalating compensation awards to their executives. We are instead directing that equity to the public benefit.</p><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">This builds on commitments our co-founders and employees have already made. When Anthropic was founded, our co-founders pledged to donate 80% of their equity holdings, and since founding we have also operated an equity donation match program that allows employees to pledge equity which Anthropic matches. Approximately half of our employees participate in this program. When combined with today’s announcement, roughly 20% of Anthropic shares will be dedicated to the public good, plus any additional percentage that could be added if the company reaches specific valuation milestones.</p><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">In the coming months, we will share more about the Anthropic Public Benefit Fund’s structure and governance, including the valuation milestones that may add to its stake. We will also report on our progress to date against our mission in an upcoming public benefit report.</p></div></div></article></div><!--$--><!--/$-->","canvases":0}